+# RL agent runtime requirements — installed into conda env "agent" by
+# Dockerfile.base. This is the WHITELIST that paperbench RL submissions
+# may depend on without violating the dependency policy.
+#
+# KEEP IN SYNC WITH: el-agent/src/utils/whitelist.py (_ALLOWED_RAW)
+# Forbidden frameworks (sb3, sb3_contrib, cleanrl, ray/rllib, tianshou,
+# torchrl, d3rlpy, DI-engine, ...) are deliberately NOT installed; agents
+# should reach for the provided lib/ or torch primitives instead.
+#
+# Scope: RL-common core only. Paper-specific environment packages (d4rl,
+# nle, isaacgym, metadrive) are NOT pre-installed for two reasons:
+#   1) baseline code rarely imports them (≤4 imports per trial across all
+#      three baseline trials, often 0); paperbench grading is code-only,
+#      so a `from d4rl import ...` line scores even if d4rl is absent at
+#      install time.
+#   2) several of those packages (mujoco_py-via-d4rl, NLE autoconf build,
+#      isaacgym NVIDIA-account wheel) are heavy / fragile; bundling them
+#      into the base image makes it slow to build and easy to break.
+# If a future experiment needs them per-paper, build a paper-specific
+# image on top of paperbench-base.
+
+# --- Numerical / DL core ------------------------------------------------
+# PyTorch CPU build (paperbench host has no GPU per code_only_instructions).
+# Pulls a ~200MB wheel rather than the ~2GB CUDA build.
+--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
+torch
+torchvision
+numpy
+scipy
+scikit-learn
+pandas
+numba
+
+# --- RL env interface (NOT a trainer framework) -------------------------
+gymnasium
+gym
+Shimmy
+mujoco
+
+# --- Visualization / logging -------------------------------------------
+matplotlib
+seaborn
+tqdm
+wandb
+tensorboard
+tensorboardX
+
+# --- Image / IO / config -----------------------------------------------
+Pillow
+opencv-python
+h5py
+joblib
+PyYAML
+omegaconf
+hydra-core
+
+# --- Misc utilities common in RL repos ---------------------------------
+einops
+absl-py
+cloudpickle
+dill
+rich
+typer
+click
+moviepy
